  "wiki.button":"Wiki","wiki.title":"Wiki","wiki.search":"Search the Wiki","wiki.noResults":"Nothing found.","wiki.related":"See also","wiki.back":"Back","wiki.info":"Open in the Wiki","wiki.free":"Free","wiki.cat.buildings":"Buildings","wiki.cat.resources":"Resources","wiki.cat.professions":"Professions","wiki.cat.animals":"Animals","wiki.cat.needs":"Needs & Happiness","wiki.cat.policy":"Policy","wiki.cat.trade":"Trade","wiki.cat.seasons":"Seasons","wiki.cat.events":"Events","wiki.fact.cost":"Price","wiki.fact.size":"Size","wiki.fact.workers":"Workers","wiki.fact.uses":"Uses","wiki.fact.makes":"Makes","wiki.fact.storage":"Storage","wiki.fact.residents":"Residents","wiki.fact.group":"Group","wiki.fact.madeIn":"Made in","wiki.fact.usedIn":"Used in","wiki.fact.skill":"Skill","wiki.fact.worksIn":"Works in","wiki.group.gold":"Gold","wiki.group.materials":"Materials","wiki.group.foodRaw":"Food ingredients","wiki.group.food":"Food","wiki.group.equipment":"Equipment","wiki.professionBody":"A {job} works in: {places}. Give the job in the Population list (the job button) or let automatic employment fill the workplace.","wiki.professionFree":"A {job} works for the whole kingdom without a workplace. Give the job in the Population list.","wiki.topic.rats.title":"Rats & Cats","wiki.topic.rats.body":"Rats move into stores with food and eat it – grain first. The fuller the store, the faster they breed. A cat living in the building catches them; a big store needs more than one cat. Take in a stray cat that comes to the village, or buy one from a Food or General merchant. Rats also move into Houses with no cat within 10 tiles, which makes the residents a little unhappy.","wiki.topic.dogs.title":"Hunting dogs","wiki.topic.dogs.body":"A stray dog can be tamed by a Hunter (the better the Hunter, the better the chance). The dog follows its Hunter: he moves faster and hits harder while the dog is close, and game near the dog can be tracked. An injured dog goes home and heals in a day. Merchants sometimes sell a dog.","wiki.topic.fire.title":"Fire","wiki.topic.fire.body":"Fires start at night once the kingdom has grown (5 Houses or the second year). A burning building needs water: residents with buckets from a Well put it out. Build Wells near the Houses and keep some residents free at night.","wiki.topic.needs.title":"Needs & Happiness","wiki.topic.needs.body":"Residents need food, a home, rest and safety. Happiness grows with varied food, a cat at home, a Village Green, a Swing Tree and a Well nearby, and feasts; it falls with hunger, unpaid wages, high taxes, small rations and rats at home. Unhappy residents work slower, strike and in the end leave.","wiki.topic.taxes.title":"Taxes & Rations","wiki.topic.taxes.body":"The Castle sets the kingdom policy. Taxes bring Gold every morning but lower happiness; rations decide how much each resident eats a day. A feast costs food and Gold and makes everyone happier for a while.","wiki.topic.trade.title":"Trade & Caravans","wiki.topic.trade.body":"With a Marketplace, merchant caravans visit every few days. Buy and sell in the trade window; Haulers carry the goods between the stores and the Marketplace. Automatic trade can buy or sell for you, or keep a good between two amounts. Caravans grow richer as the game goes on and bring porters and guards.","wiki.topic.winter.title":"Winter & Fishing","wiki.topic.winter.body":"In winter fields do not grow and fishing gives less. Fill the Granary before autumn ends: it holds 1000 food ingredients and 1000 food. Fishermen keep working on open water.","wiki.topic.builders.title":"Builders' Workshop","wiki.topic.builders.body":"Builders build every construction site in the kingdom. A Builder's Workshop gives them a place to wait between jobs. If materials are in the stores but nobody brings them, add a Hauler – or the Builders carry them themselves after a while.","tips.rats":"Rats are eating your food. Get a cat: take in a stray cat or buy one from a caravan.",
